github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6247#issuecomment-5534691466","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSeTfVg","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Nested callback order reversed <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>_request_callback_scopes</i></b> returns nested blueprint names child-first, causing URL preprocessors,\n>before-request handlers, and template context processors to run before their parent-blueprint\n>callbacks. This changes ordering-dependent results, including which before-request handler\n>short-circuits processing and which context processor value wins.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/app.py[1629]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6247/files#diff-d3e0349504081bb501c611b3954be364188a4cf442056181272e27e830ae446eR1629-R1629)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+        return (None, *ctx.request.blueprints)\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>Request.blueprints</i></b> explicitly represents the current blueprint upward through its parents, and\n><b><i>_split_blueprint_path</i></b> constructs that list starting with the complete child name before appending\n>parent names. The new helper expands this child-first list directly; its consumers iterate the tuple\n>in order for template processors, URL preprocessors, and before-request handlers.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/wrappers.py[181-195]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/23748ad3fdb7ecd77c1471084d510ac157cc85ff/src/flask/wrappers.py/#L181-L195)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/helpers.py[645-651]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/23748ad3fdb7ecd77c1471084d510ac157cc85ff/src/flask/helpers.py/#L645-L651)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[604-615]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/23748ad3fdb7ecd77c1471084d510ac157cc85ff/src/flask/app.py/#L604-L615)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[1377-1391]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/23748ad3fdb7ecd77c1471084d510ac157cc85ff/src/flask/app.py/#L1377-L1391)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[1627-1629]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/23748ad3fdb7ecd77c1471084d510ac157cc85ff/src/flask/app.py/#L1627-L1629)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The centralized request callback helper removed the reversal required for nested blueprint names. Since `Request.blueprints` is child-first, preprocessing and template callbacks now execute child scopes before parent scopes instead of preserving the existing parent-first behavior.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>Return the application scope first, followed by reversed request blueprint scopes. Add coverage using nested blueprints to verify ordering for before-request callbacks and template context processors.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/app.py[1627-1629]\n>- src/flask/wrappers.py[181-195]\n>- src/flask/helpers.py[645-651]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" heigh